@startuml save-to-fhir-sequence
!theme plain
title Save a composition -> translate to FHIR -> display the Patient Summary

skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor Clinician as U
participant "**openEHR UI**\ncomposition form" as FORM
participant "**openEHR CDR**\nEHRbase" as EHR
participant "**openFHIR**\nFHIR Connect" as OF
participant "**FHIR server**\nHAPI" as HAPI
participant "**FHIR UI**\npatient summary" as SUM

U -> FORM: Save
activate FORM

FORM -> FORM: check mandatory fields\nagainst the template
note right: A missing field is refused here.\nNothing is sent, and no pipeline is shown.

FORM -> EHR: store the composition
EHR --> FORM: committed (uid)
note right of EHR: **The save is done at this point.**\nEverything below is translation —\nif it fails, the composition still stands.

FORM -> EHR: read it back (canonical form)
EHR --> FORM: composition
note right of FORM: Canonical, because openFHIR maps\nfrom the full openEHR structure.

FORM -> OF: translate this composition
OF --> FORM: FHIR Bundle
note right of OF: Needs the template registered\nin openFHIR, not just in the CDR.

FORM -> HAPI: store the Bundle
HAPI --> FORM: Bundle id

U -> FORM: "View European Patient Summary"
FORM -> SUM: open the summary,\npassing **only the Bundle id**
deactivate FORM

activate SUM
SUM -> HAPI: fetch Bundle by id
HAPI --> SUM: Bundle
note right of SUM: Re-read rather than handed over,\nso reload and deep links work.

SUM --> U: rendered over the EPS profile —\nsections the mapping omitted\nshow as "not present"
deactivate SUM

@enduml
